{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 1 got `Verified -1`; rebuilt the split on a newer base rather than rechecking blind.\n\n**Triage of the -1.** Single failing job (macOS shard; ubuntu shards passed), single failing test: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py::test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count` — a reconciler log-capture assertion in a file this change does not touch. Mechanism read off the CI log: the per-link decline is `logger.warning` and DID appear in the captured records; the pass summary the assertion looks for is `logger.info` and did not. `caplog.at_level(logging.INFO)` raises the ROOT level, so a concurrent xdist worker leaving an above-INFO level on the reconciler logger filters the INFO summary while the WARNING still lands. Capture artifact, not behavior.\n\nThis is already filed: bug `fanatical-skittish-stud` (355b-11d4-e62c-4eb4), \"Log-capture flake in decline-count test under xdist\". Sibling change `unheedful-custodial-bluebottle` hit the identical failure in a file it likewise did not touch. Locally the same CI invocation passed 12646 tests on the patchset-1 tree, and the test passes standalone on repeated runs.\n\n**Why patchset 2 rather than a bare recheck.** `unheedful-custodial-bluebottle` (change 1713, \"Retry write-side git temp-file faults\") merged as c8a380e24c AFTER my base, and it rewrote the very region I was extracting: it deleted `_TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS`, `_GIT_ADD_BACKOFF_S`, `_is_transient_add_error` (now an alias of `gitutil._is_transient_object_write_error`) and `_with_transient_add_retry` from `event_append`, moving the family into the shared `gitutil` seam and renaming `_with_transient_head_retry` -> `_with_transient_fault_retry`. Rebasing conflicted, so I discarded my extraction and re-derived it from scratch against the new `origin/main` (@6f37d9495b) instead of hand-resolving.\n\nRe-measured on that base: `event_append.py` is **743** LOC — 1713 shaved 51, still only 57 under the cap, so the split remains warranted.\n\nRebuilt result: `event_append.py` **524**, `event_prepare.py` **145**, `event_commit_git.py` **183**. Concern boundaries unchanged; the git-verb module is smaller because the retry family now lives in `gitutil`, which it imports. Re-export list updated to match the new reality — `_with_transient_add_retry`, `_TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS` and `_GIT_ADD_BACKOFF_S` no longer exist and are gone from it; `_is_transient_add_error` and `_GIT_ADD_ATTEMPTS` moved to `event_commit_git` and are re-exported; `_with_transient_fault_retry` is retained in `event_append` for the self-heal. `gitutil.py` NOT touched.\n\nRe-verified on the new base: all five moved regions byte-identical; both new modules leaf by AST import check; no `src/rebar` file over 800; alias-aware binding completeness clean (aliases `_ea`, `_store_append`, `_store_event_append`; 21 refs; only prose false positives `NAME`/`py`/`write_lock`, none of which exist on `origin/main`'s module either); `make lint`, `make typecheck` (525 files), all 12 runnable `check_*.py` gates, complexity baseline (`new=0 increased=0`), four generators no-diff. Same `Change-Id` preserved so this is patchset 2 of change 1715, not a new change. Full suite re-running before push."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786610657689265001,"uuid":"6f4901bc-e647-47bf-99e8-58353a507c59"}